## Context

Ticket [[0876]] has 27 events with collected snapshots but no acceptable
source-line/subject pair. The bounded audit in
`docs/jetp-0876-evidence-gap-audit.md` identifies 24 Progress Report 2025
rows and three official-portal assertions. The 0875 dispositions leave their
target identities blank. Several grant labels recur across distinct source
rows; a generic project or programme name cannot stand in for each agreement.
The report's in-process financing table does not by itself establish a
physical implementation state.

This ticket handles the source-row and identity decision. The separate AfDB
event with no snapshot follows the collection path in [[0926]].

## Work

- Extract exact printed rows from Progress Report Tables 4.3-2/3/4/6/7/11
  into ledger lines, with snapshot hash and specific row locators. Reuse the
  already collected portal claim lines where their text supports the event.
- Review each proposed agreement/project identity against its source row and
  the 0875 split; keep ETP and IETF grants distinct by source row and funder.
- For each of the nine implementation assertions, record whether the printed
  text supports the claimed physical state, a weaker claim, or only financial
  pipeline status. Never infer construction or completion from financing.
- Rebuild the 0876 pending register and record one disposition per original
  event without altering its served legacy view before its own acceptance gate.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All 27 source-backed events have a precise source row, a justified
  referent (or an explicit unresolved identity decision), and a recorded
  financial/physical support verdict.
- [ ] No two distinct ETP or IETF grant rows collapse into one agreement.
- [ ] M1a served inventory bytes and the current country observation views
  remain identical until 0876 replaces them.
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, focused reconciliation tests,
  `make check-fast`, `make lint`, and full `make check` are run; inherited
  failures are identified separately.
